---
import "../styles/site.css";

/** What the product does, in the same terms the reference pages use. */
const capabilities = [
  {
    title: "One document per workspace",
    body: "The workspace is a Loro CRDT. Edits merge without a server in the loop, and a relay syncs peers when one is reachable.",
  },
  {
    title: "Typed cards on a canvas",
    body: "Cards, boards, sections, types, tags and edges live in one object graph, and Zod validates every write before it reaches the document.",
  },
  {
    title: "Every card is an editor",
    body: "Text, checklists, fields and templates are edited in place with Tiptap, so a card holds the work and not a link to it.",
  },
  {
    title: "Sharing without an account",
    body: "A share link serves a read-only projection of a board or a card. A link with edit rights works on a draft and publishes the diff back.",
  },
];

/**
 * The hosted plans, from the tier table the licence is minted from
 * (`services/billing/src/stripe/tiers.ts`, published in
 * `docs/reference/billing.md`). A licence carries a seat count, a workspace count
 * and two storage caps; nothing on this page is a price. Both plans sell one seat,
 * so a plan is one person and the names say so (ADR-0082).
 */
const plans = [
  { name: "Solo", seats: "1", workspaces: "3", documentBytes: "256 MiB", attachmentBytes: "1 GiB" },
  {
    name: "Solo Pro",
    seats: "1",
    workspaces: "25",
    documentBytes: "2 GiB",
    attachmentBytes: "8 GiB",
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Suite: a local-first canvas for connected notes</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Suite is a local-first canvas. A workspace is one Loro document of typed cards, edited offline in the browser and synced by a relay when one is reachable."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://suite.run/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Suite" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://suite.run/" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="A local-first canvas of typed cards, edited offline and synced when a relay is reachable."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">
        <span class="wordmark-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Suite
      </a>
      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Suite">
        <a href="https://docs.suite.run">Docs</a>
        <a href="https://app.suite.run">Open the app</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-rogers-neighborhood/suite-canvas">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Beta</p>
        <h1>A canvas that keeps the connections you drew.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          A workspace is one document of typed cards. Write in it, place it on a board, link it to
          another card, and everything you did not write yourself is recomputed on read.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="https://app.suite.run">Open Suite</a>
          <a class="button" href="https://docs.suite.run">Read the docs</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">
          No account for local use. The app runs in the browser, saves to IndexedDB, and needs a relay
          only to sync with someone else.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="capabilities" aria-labelledby="what-it-does">
        <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
        <div class="capability-grid">
          {
            capabilities.map((capability) => (
              <article class="capability">
                <h3>{capability.title}</h3>
                <p>{capability.body}</p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="offline" aria-labelledby="offline">
        <h2 id="offline">Offline is the default, not a mode</h2>
        <p>
          Edits go to the open tab first and reach the network afterwards. A workspace opens from the
          local snapshot, so a dropped connection pauses sync and nothing else. Reloading while
          offline needs the network, because the app ships no service worker, and that limit is stated
          in the interface rather than discovered.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing">
        <h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2>
        <p class="pricing-lede">
          Two hosted plans are configured, one seat each. A licence carries a seat count, a workspace
          count and two storage caps, and the relay enforces the tighter of the licence and the
          instance.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Plan</th>
              <th scope="col">Seats</th>
              <th scope="col">Workspaces</th>
              <th scope="col">Document bytes per workspace</th>
              <th scope="col">Attachment bytes per workspace</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              plans.map((plan) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">{plan.name}</th>
                  <td>{plan.seats}</td>
                  <td>{plan.workspaces}</td>
                  <td>{plan.documentBytes}</td>
                  <td>{plan.attachmentBytes}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="pricing-note">
          Hosted subscriptions are not on sale yet. When they are, a plan is one person: inviting a
          second member is refused rather than billed, because seats are not sold separately.
          Self-hosting needs no licence: the same quotas are environment variables, and unset means
          unlimited.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="selfhost" aria-labelledby="self-host">
        <h2 id="self-host">Self-host it</h2>
        <p>
          One Compose file brings up the static app, the relay that syncs workspaces, and Caddy in front
          of them. The relay keeps its documents in SQLite on a named volume, so a backup is that volume
          and nothing else.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://docs.suite.run/how-to/deploy/">Deployment guide</a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>Suite is a local-first canvas, MIT licensed.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Elsewhere">
        <a href="https://app.suite.run">app.suite.run</a>
        <a href="https://docs.suite.run">docs.suite.run</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-rogers-neighborhood/suite-canvas">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
